 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication and roles
+
+Every request requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are configured in
+`apiKeys` in the data file, each with `key`, `name`, and `role`.
+Missing, malformed, or unknown keys return 401 (`unauthorized`); insufficient
+permission returns 403 (`forbidden`), both in the usual error shape.
+
+Viewers may use GET routes except `/audit`. Cooks may also POST to
+`/recipes/:id/cook`, `/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures`, and
+`/stocktakes/:id/counts`. Managers may use every route.
+
+## Routes
+
+All routes are listed under Routes in `README.md`.
+`GET /audit` returns an array of audit entries newest first, for managers only.
+Each saved write records `time` (ISO instant), `keyName`, `method`, `path`
+(including any query string), and response `status`. Reads and rejected writes
+that do not save data do not add entries. The data and audit entry save together.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
